      "author": "Marvelcanon1",
      "credit": "Own work",
      "attribution": "",
      "description": "Route directly connecting waystations of a flying palace (Pushpaka vimana) in Hindu legends. The route (of Rama, Sita, Laxmana and their company) starts at the tip of Sri Lanka, where Maldives is located on the West side of it. The dotted-line which is connected to Lanka is a drowned landmass due to rise in sea level or other effects. The second stop is at the top of the bottom tip of India. The third stop is at the Malaya mountains. The fourth stop is at Mahendragiri. The fifth stop is at Anegundi (village). The sixth stop is at Panchavati. The seventh stop is at Lonar (lake). The eighth stop is Ramtek. The ninth stop is at Jabalpur. The tenth stop is at Chitrakoot. The eleventh stop is at Nandigram (village in Uttar Pradesh). The twelfth stop is at Ayodhya (hometown). The last place is at Allahabad, officially known as Prayagraj.",
